&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic&#39;s community spans developers building new products, individual Claude users, and practitioners and buyers inside enterprise accounts — from the staff engineer using Claude Code to C-Suite decision-makers. We&#39;re hiring a Head of Community to turn our current set of programs into a function that helps millions of people build real skills with Claude, measurably growing retained users and product adoption.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead and grow a global team that covers ambassadors programs, regional community leads, and enterprise champion programs. Your job is to give this team a sharp operating model and a measurement framework that ladders our initiatives to business outcomes, so users can get the most out of Claude. You&#39;ll build community across audiences, seniority levels, functions, and roles: enterprise buyers and executive sponsors, developers and technical practitioners, and the knowledge workers in between. This role sits at the intersection of Product, Sales, PMM, Brand, and Comms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the global community strategy and operating model: the audience thesis, the portfolio of programs, and what&#39;s built centrally vs. run in-region&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead, coach, and scale a global team of program and regional owners; hire the gaps, set the bar, and develop community-native operators&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define the measurement framework that replaces activity metrics: partner with Product and Data Science to define success metrics and segment the base (non-user → occasional → high-value daily) — with recurring retained users and product adoption as the top-line outcomes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build community across the full range of audiences and seniority levels, with programs and voice tuned to each without fragmenting the experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect bottoms-up adoption to enterprise expansion: architect the champions, train-the-trainer, and partner ecosystem motions that turn power users inside accounts into org-wide adoption, and integrate them into how Sales and CS run strategic account plans&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bring training, certification, enablement, and community help together into one engine that scales through champions and partners — so users experience a single path to skill-building with Claude&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner tightly with Brand and Comms to keep sentiment and awareness healthy: define where community shows up in Anthropic&#39;s brand and how we best serve our users&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Align community strategy proactively with product direction, launches, and pricing &amp;amp; packaging — owning community&#39;s job pre-launch, at launch, and post-launch, and proving it drives value for our users&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have built and led a community or customer advocacy function at a company where community was a growth lever, not a cost center — and can point to the retention, adoption, or expansion outcomes it drove&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have led and developed a distributed team of program owners and regional leads accountable for commercial impact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think in funnels and segments as naturally as you think in programs: you&#39;re comfortable putting your name on a metric in a QBR and defending how community moved it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have connected self-serve, bottoms-up adoption inside large accounts to enterprise expansion, and can articulate exactly where community sits in that motion&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Can flex your playbook across very different audiences — a technical, API-first developer community and an enterprise executive buyer community are different jobs, and you&#39;ve done versions of both&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operate as an integrated marketer: you&#39;ve worked day-to-day with cross-functional teams and have strong opinions about how community stays customer-first&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are comfortable partnering with Product and Data Science to define usage quality, instrument it, and hold your team to it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Write and communicate clearly, hold a room with both a Staff engineer and a CIO, and are energized by ambiguity and building at speed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run community or advocacy at a company operating both a PLG / self-serve motion and an enterprise sales motion at the same time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built or led a recognized champions, ambassadors, or advocacy program at a company known for the model&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with developer tools, infrastructure, or AI products, and credibility with technical audiences&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built the measurement plumbing for a community function before including cohorting, attribution, and usage segmentation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;International experience standing up or scaling community in-region (EMEA, Japan/APAC) with a clear philosophy on what runs centrally vs. locally&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of listening to communities and building user trust through hard moments alongside a Comms team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Background spanning more than one of: community, customer marketing, developer relations, customer education/enablement, or growth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The annual compensation range for this role is listed below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For sales roles, the range provided is the role’s On Target Earnings (&quot;OTE&quot;) range, meaning that the range includes both the sales commissions/sales bonuses target and annual base salary for the role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$400,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$400,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum education: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, and/or experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required field of study:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A field relevant to the role as demonstrated through coursework, training, or professional experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum years of experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Years of experience required will correlate with the internal job level requirements for the position&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location-based hybrid policy:&lt;/strong&gt; Currently, we expect all staff to be in one of our offices at least 25% of the time. However, some roles may require more time in our offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We do sponsor visas! However, we aren&#39;t able to successfully sponsor visas for every role and every candidate. But if we make you an offer, we will make every reasonable effort to get you a visa, and we retain an immigration lawyer to help with this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We encourage you to apply even if you do not believe you meet every single qualification.&lt;/strong&gt; Not all strong candidates will meet every single qualification as listed.&amp;nbsp; Research shows that people who identify as being from underrepresented groups are more prone to experiencing imposter syndrome and doubting the strength of their candidacy, so we urge you not to exclude yourself prematurely and to submit an application if you&#39;re interested in this work. We think AI systems like the ones we&#39;re building have enormous social and ethical implications. We think this makes representation even more important, and we strive to include a range of diverse perspectives on our team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Your safety matters to us.&lt;/strong&gt; To protect yourself from potential scams, remember that Anthropic recruiters only contact you from&amp;nbsp;@anthropic.com&amp;nbsp;email addresses. In some cases, we may partner with vetted recruiting agencies who will identify themselves as working on behalf of Anthropic. Be cautious of emails from other domains. Legitimate Anthropic recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before your first day. If you&#39;re ever unsure about a communication, don&#39;t click any links—visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;http://anthropic.com/careers&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot; data-remove-tab-index=&quot;true&quot;&gt;anthropic.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;directly for confirmed position openings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we&#39;re different&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that the highest-impact AI research will be big science. At Anthropic we work as a single cohesive team on just a few large-scale research efforts. And we value impact — advancing our long-term goals of steerable, trustworthy AI — rather than work on smaller and more specific puzzles. We view AI research as an empirical science, which has as much in common with physics and biology as with traditional efforts in computer science. We&#39;re an extremely collaborative group, and we host frequent research discussions to ensure that we are pursuing the highest-impact work at any given time. As such, we greatly value communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to understand our research directions is to read our recent research. This research continues many of the directions our team worked on prior to Anthropic, including: GPT-3, Circuit-Based Interpretability, Multimodal Neurons, Scaling Laws, AI &amp;amp; Compute, Concrete Problems in AI Safety, and Learning from Human Preferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come work with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic is a public benefit corporation headquartered in San Francisco. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, optional equity donation matching, generous vacation and parental leave, flexible working hours, and a lovely office space in which to collaborate with colleagues. &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Guidance on Candidates&#39; AI Usage:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Learn about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.anthropic.com/candidate-ai-guidance&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;our policy&lt;/a&gt; for using AI in our application process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Anthropic&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Anthropic’s mission is to create reliable, interpretable, and steerable AI systems. We want AI to be safe and beneficial for our users and for society as a whole. Our team is a quickly growing group of committed researchers, engineers, policy experts, and business leaders working together to build beneficial AI systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The world&#39;s engineers want to get the most out of Claude. At Anthropic, technical instruction already happens everywhere: our Applied AI and Forward Deployed Engineering teams teach customers and partners, and engineers across the company help others learn to build with Claude. Today that instruction is a shared responsibility, delivered alongside people&#39;s primary roles. As demand grows, we need to turn that distributed expertise into a dedicated technical instruction function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build that function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the first person at Anthropic whose full-time job is technical instruction. You&#39;ll spend your first year primarily in the classroom teaching engineers, architects, and other technical practitioners. You&#39;ll also build the people, standards, and systems that let Anthropic&#39;s technical instruction scale far beyond the people we directly employ.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a player-coach role. From day one you manage a small bench of instructors. You set the bar for what &quot;ready to teach&quot; means, decide who is cleared to teach a given module in Anthropic&#39;s technical programs, and assess facilitators from our training partners against that bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re an engineer who teaches and a teacher who has led other teachers. You can build an agent live in front of a skeptical engineer, diagnose what isn&#39;t working in a technical lab, and make the material better. You can also watch an experienced instructor teach, tell them their session isn&#39;t ready yet, and coach them to get there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to the Head of Technical Enablement. The role is based in San Francisco with some travel expected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead from the front.&lt;/strong&gt; Teach hands-on sessions to new Applied AI engineers, our field teams, and partner cohorts, in rooms from 12-person labs to 100-person training days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the instructor bench.&lt;/strong&gt; Hire and develop instructors and curriculum developers. Decide contract renewals, and recommend conversions to full-time, against criteria you define.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the quality bar.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the observation rubric, dry-run protocol, and cleared-to-teach process for every instructor-led technical session.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale through train-the-trainer.&lt;/strong&gt; Set the bar the Lead Technical Instructor&#39;s train-the-trainer program teaches to, for internal experts, contract instructors, and partner facilitators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn expertise into instruction.&lt;/strong&gt; Turn internal experts&#39; content into sessions and labs that work in a live room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable programs without owning them.&lt;/strong&gt; Staff other teams&#39; programs with cleared instructors, and own the quality of instruction inside them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure and improve.&lt;/strong&gt; Report learner pass rates per instructor each month, and act on them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years of relevant professional experience&lt;/strong&gt; across software engineering, solutions engineering, developer advocacy, technical education, or related technical roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4+ years of hands-on technical instruction.&lt;/strong&gt; You have taught engineers live and hands-on, across audience sizes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production engineering.&lt;/strong&gt; You have written and shipped production software and engage credibly with experienced engineers on architecture and debugging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recent hands-on AI development.&lt;/strong&gt; In your last three years of work, you have built or debugged applications with LLM APIs, agent frameworks, tool use, MCP, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; You have managed instructors, trainers, developer advocates, or solutions engineers, including hiring and performance management, and kept teaching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instructor development.&lt;/strong&gt; You have designed or run a train-the-trainer program, instructor certification, or observation framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;San Francisco location.&lt;/strong&gt; You are based in San Francisco or willing to relocate with our relocation support, can be in the office every day a program runs, 3 days in a normal week, and can travel 25 to 30 percent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio of sessions you taught and a rubric or certification you designed, shared only if you have the right.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building an instruction or developer-education function from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a contractor instructor bench, or clearing instructors across regions from recordings or trained observers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily use of Claude Code or a comparable agentic coding tool, or building on Claude through Amazon Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, or Microsoft Foundry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep enthusiasm for AI and real care about building it responsibly.&lt;/li&gt;
